## Custom configuration
{{- end -}}

{{- define "custom.custom.configuration" -}}
{{ template "custom.custom.configuration.header" . }}

[matterjs-server](https://github.com/matter-js/matterjs-server) is the Open
Home Foundation Matter Server built on matter.js, and the successor of the
archived python-matter-server. It is a drop-in replacement with the same
WebSocket API: point Home Assistant's Matter integration at
`ws://<release>.<namespace>.svc:5580/ws`.

### Moving from python-matter-server

Use the same data directory: the first start migrates it (see the upstream
[migration guide](https://github.com/matter-js/matterjs-server/blob/main/docs/migration.md)).
The new image runs as uid 1000, not root, so the files must be owned by
1000:1000. `fsGroup` handles group access on most volume types; otherwise run
`chown -R 1000:1000` on the volume once.

### Networking

Matter devices and Thread border routers are reached over IPv6 (link-local
and ULA) and discovered with mDNS, so the server must be on the same LAN as
the devices.

**Host network (default):** simplest; set `PRIMARY_INTERFACE` if the node has
several interfaces.

**Multus:** to give the server its own address on the LAN, attach a macvlan
interface, turn host networking off and select that interface. Thread devices
are reached through the border router, so the pod also needs a route to the
Thread prefix (taken from the router advertisements, or added explicitly).

```yaml
defaultPodOptions:
  hostNetwork: false
  dnsPolicy: ClusterFirst
  annotations:
    k8s.v1.cni.cncf.io/networks: |
      [{"name": "lan", "namespace": "kube-system",
        "ips": ["192.168.1.22/24"], "mac": "c6:5e:a4:00:00:22"}]

controllers:
  main:
    containers:
      main:
        env:
          PRIMARY_INTERFACE: net1
```

### Bluetooth commissioning

Set `bluetooth.adapter` (e.g. `0` for hci0). The chart then mounts the host's
`/run/dbus` read-only and uses the BlueZ D-Bus backend, which keeps the
container unprivileged. The node must run `bluetoothd` with the adapter powered,
so pin the pod to that node. Commissioning through the Home Assistant
companion app needs no Bluetooth on the server at all.
{{- end -}}
